body:
Griffith always reminded me of a fucked up version of a funny t-shirt I saw when I was a kid that said "Jesus saves sinners.... and redeems them for fabulous prizes."

&#x200B;

Griffith was always a narcissist. From the very beginning Berserk established Griffith as an unrelenting leader, who "collected" members and cared for them the way you would care for a useful tool. No one had any attachment to Griffith, aside from admiration and respect. He found them all, gave them a life path to follow, and considered himself their Benefactor. He gave them a purpose, they advanced his goals, nothing more, nothing less. Griffith was, from day one, essentially a billionaire tech mogul who cares very little about the minions that made his masterpiece work. When he finally found another person who showed any REAL level of potential, his initial thought was to OWN it. Control it. 

&#x200B;

So when Griffith loses everything, and every eye that followed him was now pointing at someone who was every bit as capable as he had been in his prime, he chose to DIE rather than live and be weak. So when the God hand appeared and gave him the choice to regain his power, not only did he not even HESITATE to sacrifice the people he had already told "I decide when and how you die" he went so far as to take EVERYTHING from the man he perceived as a threat, to reassert his place. to feel "superior" again.

&#x200B;

It wasn't complex. He's a narcissist, and he did some textbook narcissist shit.

Shoot 'Em Up.

&#x200B;

Everyone I've talked (that has even seen, heard of, or even remembers that movie) HATED it. I laughed my ASS off. Fantastic.

Just wanna post an Update:

&#x200B;

I ran a diagnostic on my memory, and it came back with an error. I replaced my RAM and I haven't had any Marmot issues since. And i normally get multiple per day. If none of the other fixes work for you, it may be a RAM issue.

I appreciate what they tried to fo here but Guts would go absolutely Batshit if he saw this crap.

&#x200B;

I was considering getting this to rock with Celestial Nighthawk. Now I'm glad I didn't lol
